			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Accept numeric handles in FileWatcher and improve 404 detection\n\nTwo changes in Mountain's gRPC service layer:\n\n1. **FileWatcher.rs**: Cocoon's `NextProviderHandle()` returns a number, but older callers pass a string. Handle both shapes in `RegisterWatcher` and `UnregisterWatcher` instead of silently converting numbers to empty string.\n\n2. **MountainVinegRPCService.rs**: Extend 404-like error detection to include `FileSystem.ReadDirectory` and additional error message patterns (\"no such file or directory\", \"entity not found\", \"os error 2\"). Return distinct error code `-32004` for benign 404s so Cocoon's shim can classify them without a string-regex round-trip, while `-32000` remains the catch-all for genuine failures.",
			"SHA": "160b5a4251133f31e4ce99898a02a8d63f8ca19b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T01:03:45Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				859,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Mountain): Update build.rs comments to document PascalCase naming\n\nClarify the build script comments to document the PascalCase environment variable naming convention introduced in the 2026-04-29 migration. The comments now specify that `Profile`, `Pack`, `Bundle`, and `Compiler` (PascalCase) are the current env var names, replacing the legacy `LAND_*` names that were retired. This ensures clarity for developers debugging build configuration resolution at runtime.",
			"SHA": "de696659a367b81cdc5404e3055fa6837bd94fa7"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-28T23:06:33Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				859,
				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Add per-URI marker payloads to diagnostics events and cap keyring logging\n\nTwo changes in Mountain's diagnostic system:\n\n1. **DiagnosticProvider.rs**: Extend the `DiagnosticsChanged` event payload with a new `changedURIs` field containing per-URI marker data alongside the existing `Uris` string array. This enables SkyBridge's `cel:diagnostics:changed` listener to call `IMarkerService.changeOne(owner, uri, markers)` directly without an extra IPC round-trip per diagnostic change. Also adds lowercase `owner` field for consistency. Maintains backward compatibility with listeners expecting the original format.\n\n2. **LoggingPlugin.rs**: Cap the `keyring` crate to Warn level. This dependency (used by Mountain's secret-storage path for license data lookups) emits a 3-line DEBUG block per `get_password` call that fires indefinitely after the workbench paints, similar to the previous `ignore` and `globset` mutes.\n\nSigned-off-by: Nikola Hristov <Nikola@PlayForm.Cloud>",
			"SHA": "5b111b189f5566e92bce268a48be289d73ef6735"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-28T22:00:38Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				859,
				4
			],
			"Message": "refactor: simplify project naming in Cargo.toml and tauri.conf.json\n\nSigned-off-by: Nikola Hristov <Nikola@PlayForm.Cloud>",
			"SHA": "7ecd2c78579c71c6c6dbbbb509d52c63b1e771ad"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-28T21:54:13Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				861,
				6
			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Resolve 404s for extension webview assets and reduce logging noise\n\nTwo bug fixes in Mountain's build modules:\n\n1. **Scheme.rs**: Extend vscode-file URI handling to support arbitrary authorities beyond \"vscode-app\". The original code only handled `vscode-file://vscode-app/<path>` but `WebviewImplementation::asWebviewUri` rewrites local resource URIs to use the extension's identifier as authority (e.g., `vscode-file://vscode.git/...`). This caused every extension-supplied webview asset (icons, scripts, stylesheets, fonts) to return 404. Added a generic fallback that extracts the path after any authority.\n\n2. **LoggingPlugin.rs**: Cap noisy extension-scanner log targets (\"ignore\", \"ignore::walk\", \"ignore::gitignore\", \"globset\") to Warn level. These crates emit DEBUG lines per `.gitignore` opened, per glob compiled, and per file whitelisted—tens of thousands during a single boot, drowning out extension activation signals.\n\nAlso updates binary/lib names and tauri productName to include build configuration identifiers for development builds.",
			"SHA": "bbbdab26d47fbd3bca35342c224431194c519eb7"
		}
	],
